error[E0277]: a 204 or a 205 says there is no body, and a `String` is a value that the route answers
  --> tests/compile_fail_server/no_content_of_a_value.rs:17:53
   |
17 |         Ok(Response::new(String::new()).with_status(Status::NO_CONTENT))
   |                                         ----------- ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a status of no content, on a value `String`
   |                                         |
   |                                         required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `Allows<String>` is not implemented for `rest::response::sealed::NoBody`
   = note: a handler's value that may answer no content is an `Option`: `Option<String>` in place of `String` in the contract, `-> Option<String>`, `-> Created<Option<String>>` or `-> Accepted<Option<String>>`, and `Response::new(None)` with this status in the handler
   = help: `rest::response::sealed::NoBody` implements trait `Allows<T>`:
             Allows<()>
             Allows<ByteStream>
             Allows<Events<T>>
             Allows<JsonLines<T>>
             Allows<Option<T>>
             Allows<Text>
             Allows<quoll::rest::Bytes>
note: required by a bound in `Response::<T>::with_status`
  --> src/rest/response.rs
   |
   | impl<T> Response<T> {
...
   |     pub fn with_status<S>(mut self, status: S) -> Self
...
   |         S::Body: Allows<T>,
   |                  ^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `Response::<T>::with_status`
